<td id="mwAnY">Nye received the Candle in the Dark Award for his "lively, creative... endeavor". Aykroyd "was presented in absentia the Snuffed Candle Award for hosting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Psi_Factor" title="Psi Factor" id="mwAnc">Psi Factor</a> and being a "long-time promoter ... of paranormal claims" Following the awards, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Joe_Nickell" title="Joe Nickell" id="mwAng">Joe Nickell</a> wrote to Aykroyd asking for the research behind the "cases" presented on Psi Factor. Particularly a claim that NASA scientists were "killed while investigating a meteor crash and giant eggs were found and incubated, yielding a flea the size of a hog".<sup about="#mwt211" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Candle_awards_1997_60-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Candle awards 1997"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Candle_awards_1997-60"}}'><a href="./Committee_for_Skeptical_Inquiry#cite_note-Candle_awards_1997-60" id="mwAnk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAno"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAns">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnw">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr>
