</section><section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwA70"><h3 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Responsibility_in_Journalism_Award">Responsibility in Journalism Award</h3>
<p id="mwA74">CSICOP seeking to acknowledge and encourage "fair and balanced reporting of paranormal claims" established the Responsibility in Journalism Award in 1984. Frazier stated that "There are many responsible reporters who want to do a good job in covering these kinds of controversial, exotic topics."<sup about="#mwt280" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hook_award_1985_40-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hook award 1985"}}'><a href="./Committee_for_Skeptical_Inquiry#cite_note-Hook_award_1985-40" id="mwA78"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8E">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8I">]</span></span></a></sup> Beginning in 1991, CSI began awarding in two categories, "print" and "broadcast".<sup about="#mwt281" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-1991_Awards_47-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"1991 Awards"}}'><a href="./Committee_for_Skeptical_Inquiry#cite_note-1991_Awards-47" id="mwA8M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8U">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8Y">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

